// There are three ways to resume a thread: 1. By thread_id: load the thread from
// disk by thread_id and resume it. 2. By history: instantiate the thread from
// memory and resume it. 3. By path: load the thread from disk by path and resume
// it.
//
// For non-running threads, the precedence is: history > non-empty path >
// thread_id. If using history or a non-empty path for a non-running thread, the
// thread_id param will be ignored.
//
// If thread_id identifies a running thread, app-server rejoins that thread and
// treats a non-empty path as a consistency check against the active rollout path.
// Empty string path values are treated as absent.
//
// Prefer using thread_id whenever possible.

type ThreadResumeParamsBaseInstructions *string

